  "files": [
    {
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n    int n,s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n    assert(s<n);\n    assert(n<8000);\n    assert(s>0);\n    assert(n>0);\n\n    std::vector<long long> colPref(n * n);\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;++j) {\n            long long running = 0;\n            for(int i=0;i<n;++i) {\n                running += matrix[i][j];\n                colPref[i*n + j] = running;\n            }\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(dynamic, 1)\n        for(int r=0; r<=n-s; ++r) {\n            int bottom = r + s - 1;\n            int topMinusOne = r - 1;\n            long long cur = 0;\n            for(int c=0;c<s;++c) {\n                long long seg = colPref[bottom*n + c] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topMinusOne*n + c] : 0);\n                cur += seg;\n            }\n            if(cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur;\n\n            for(int c=1; c<=n-s; ++c) {\n                int outCol = c-1;\n                int inCol = c+s-1;\n                long long segOut = colPref[bottom*n + outCol] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topMinusOne*n + outCol] : 0);\n                long long segIn = colPref[bottom*n + inCol] - (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topMinusOne*n + inCol] : 0);\n                cur += segIn - segOut;\n                if(cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining the two separate OpenMP parallel regions into a single #pragma omp parallel block reduces thread creation and fork/join overhead, while switching the row-parallel loop from static to dynamic scheduling with chunk size 1 improves load balance across threads at fine granularity. This should lower overall execution time on the 4-core target.",
  "notes": "The transformation preserves all algorithmic logic and correctness. The column-prefix-sum computation remains statically scheduled for good cache locality, while the row loop uses dynamic scheduling to adapt to any minor per-row runtime variation. Only src/solution.cpp is modified; no other files are touched.",
